# Long Term Roadmap — Epics (Planner)

**Layer 2 of 4 — the epics.** The multi-sprint arc: bodies of work large
enough to need their own sprint (or several), sitting between the project
objectives in [goals.md](goals.md) and the current sprint spec. Order
roughly by leverage/cost, not strict priority.

**This file holds only what is NOT yet scoped into a sprint.** When an epic
gets scoped, the Architect writes it up as a spec in `docs/specs/` and this
file's entry collapses to a one-line pointer at that spec. That collapse is
the point: an epic described in full here *and* specified in a spec is two
sources of truth, and the unversioned one will drift (this file lives under
`.friday/active/`, which is gitignored; the spec is versioned in the project
repo).

Scoping detail that would be useful to the Architect later — anchors, source
material, the shape a derivation should take — is welcome here **while the
epic is unscoped**. It is carried into the spec when the epic is scoped, and
pruned from here at the same time.

